  "interpretation": "All 128 sampled body/direction groups contain an uphill fixed-pose interval; their first intervals begin at 10 to 35 degrees from inverted. The best original controller-boundary progress per body is 11.398 to 14.392 degrees. These posthoc observations motivate testing momentum accumulation and non-complementary multi-phase limb coordination; they do not establish the cause of failure or a dynamic barrier bound.",
  "next_gate": "Use the retained geometry witnesses to design distinct wind-up, drive and catch poses with independent limb timing and measured momentum/work accounting. Qualify the changed controller and its smallest necessary native route, then search a broad body/controller cohort from a clean pushed freeze with unchanged physical limits and upright criteria. Fresh varied-start confirmation and complete Godot handoffs remain necessary for useful candidates.",
  "limits": [
    "Finite sampled geometry only; no continuous pose, orientation or morphology coverage.",
    "Each five-degree comparison holds its joint pose fixed. Transitions between selected witness poses, their joint work and contact-force feasibility are not modeled.",
